# Jev TypeSafe routing

Jev is TypeSafe's System One model. It is not a chat model and must not be used as a Cursor `model` ID. It classifies and scores; Cursor LLMs write code.

## Before launching a subagent

A user hook already calls Jev on every `Task` tool use and may rewrite `subagent_type`. Do not set `model` to `jev`, `jev-latest`, or `typesafe-ai/jev`.

If you need an explicit routing preview, call MCP `jev_route` with a short task summary (never secrets or a full transcript).

## Typed judgments

When a decision is a closed set, a yes/no, or a rubric score, call MCP `jev_ask` instead of prompt-and-parse:

- `choice` — pick one option from criteria you define
- `score` — rate against ordered levels
- `noul` — probability that a statement is true (0–1)

Keep questions atomic. Combine answers in code. Do not send API keys, `.env` contents, credentials, or full chat transcripts as `state`.
